### ==================================================================
### MANGA SERIES
### ==================================================================

### Create a manga series
POST http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Berserk",
  "author": "Kentaro Miura",
  "totalVolumes": null
}

> {%
    client.global.set("berserkSeriesId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get all manga series
GET http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series

### Get the series just created
GET http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/{{berserkSeriesId}}

### Get a series that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/999

### Update the series -> every field changed from creation, not just totalVolumes, to actually exercise
### every setter (see the missing setArtist bug caught on the LightNovel vertical: a PUT test that reuses
### creation-time values can pass even though a setter is silently broken)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/{{berserkSeriesId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Berserk (edited)",
  "author": "Kentaro Miura (edited)",
  "totalVolumes": 41
}

### Update a series that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter",
  "totalVolumes": 1
}

### Create with blank name and author -> expect 400 with fieldError map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "author": "",
  "totalVolumes": 1
}

### Delete the series
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/{{berserkSeriesId}}

### Get the deleted series -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/{{berserkSeriesId}}


### ==================================================================
### MANGA
### ==================================================================

### Create a fresh series for the manga tests below
POST http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vinland Saga",
  "author": "Makoto Yukimura",
  "totalVolumes": 27
}

> {%
    client.global.set("vinlandSagaSeriesId", response.body.id);
%}

### Create a standalone manga (no series)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/mangas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Solo Leveling, Vol. 1",
  "author": "Chugong",
  "synopsis": "The weakest hunter in the world gains the power to level up without limit.",
  "coverImageUrl": null,
  "publishedDate": "2018-03-04",
  "totalChapters": 5,
  "volumeNumber": null,
  "genres": ["ISEKAI", "FANTASY"],
  "artist": "Dubu (REDICE STUDIO)",
  "totalPages": 192
}

> {%
    client.global.set("soloLevelingMangaId", response.body.id);
%}

### Create a manga attached to the series above
POST http://localhost:8080/api/mangas?seriesId={{vinlandSagaSeriesId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Vinland Saga, Vol. 1",
  "author": "Makoto Yukimura",
  "synopsis": "A young Viking seeks revenge against the mercenary who killed his father.",
  "coverImageUrl": null,
  "publishedDate": "2013-11-12",
  "totalChapters": 6,
  "volumeNumber": 1,
  "genres": ["FANTASY"],
  "artist": "Makoto Yukimura",
  "totalPages": 424
}

> {%
    client.global.set("vinlandSagaMangaId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get all mangas
GET http://localhost:8080/api/mangas

### Get the standalone manga -> series should be null
GET http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/{{soloLevelingMangaId}}

### Get the series-linked manga -> series should be populated
GET http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/{{vinlandSagaMangaId}}

### Get a manga that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/999

### Create a manga with a non-existent seriesId -> expect 404 (MangaSeriesNotFoundException)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/mangas?seriesId=999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter"
}

### Create a manga with blank title and author -> expect 400 with fieldError map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/mangas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "author": ""
}

### Update the standalone manga, attaching it to the series too -> every field deliberately changed from
### creation (not just artist/totalPages/volumeNumber), to actually exercise every setter (see the missing
### setArtist bug caught on the LightNovel vertical: a PUT test that reuses creation-time values can pass
### even though a setter is silently broken)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/{{soloLevelingMangaId}}?seriesId={{vinlandSagaSeriesId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Solo Leveling, Vol. 1 (edited)",
  "author": "Chugong (edited)",
  "synopsis": "The weakest hunter in the world gains a mysterious power to level up without limit.",
  "coverImageUrl": "https://covers.example.com/solo-leveling-vol1.jpg",
  "publishedDate": "2018-03-11",
  "totalChapters": 6,
  "volumeNumber": 2,
  "genres": ["ISEKAI", "FANTASY", "ACTION"],
  "artist": "Jang Sung-rak",
  "totalPages": 200
}

### Update a manga that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter"
}

### Try deleting the series while mangas still reference it -> expect the RESTRICT FK to kick in (409)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/{{vinlandSagaSeriesId}}

### Delete both mangas
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/{{soloLevelingMangaId}}

### Delete the other manga
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/mangas/{{vinlandSagaMangaId}}

### Now nothing references the series -> delete should succeed this time
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/manga-series/{{vinlandSagaSeriesId}}


### ==================================================================
### USER MANGA (tracking)
### ==================================================================

### Register a dedicated user for the tracking tests below, so this file can run standalone
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manga-tracker",
  "password": "supersecret",
  "email": "manga-tracker@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("mangaTrackerUserId", response.body.id);
%}

### Create a fresh standalone manga to track
POST http://localhost:8080/api/mangas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "One Piece, Vol. 1",
  "author": "Eiichiro Oda",
  "synopsis": "A boy with rubber powers sets out to become the King of the Pirates.",
  "coverImageUrl": null,
  "publishedDate": "1997-12-24",
  "totalChapters": 8,
  "volumeNumber": null,
  "genres": ["FANTASY", "MARTIAL_ARTS"],
  "artist": "Eiichiro Oda",
  "totalPages": 208
}

> {%
    client.global.set("onePieceMangaId", response.body.id);
%}

### Start tracking the manga above
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/mangas/{{onePieceMangaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READING",
  "rating": null,
  "currentChapter": 4,
  "currentPage": 90
}

> {%
    client.global.set("userMangaWorkId", response.body.id);
%}

### List the READING tab -> should include the tracking record just created
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works?status=READING

### List the FINISHED tab -> should be empty
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works?status=FINISHED

### Track the same manga again for the same user -> expect 409 (DuplicateTrackingException)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/mangas/{{onePieceMangaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READING",
  "rating": null,
  "currentChapter": 1,
  "currentPage": 1
}

### Track for a user that doesn't exist -> expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/999/mangas/{{onePieceMangaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PLAN_TO_READ"
}

### Track a manga that doesn't exist -> expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/mangas/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PLAN_TO_READ"
}

### Update progress only -> status/rating should stay untouched
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userMangaWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentChapter": 6,
  "currentPage": 140
}

### Update just the rating -> chapter/page from above should be unaffected
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userMangaWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 9
}

### Update the status -> currentChapter/currentPage/rating from above should be unaffected; also the first
### test in this file to actually exercise UserWorkController applying request.status()
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userMangaWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "FINISHED"
}

### Update with an out-of-range rating -> expect 400 (validation runs on PATCH too)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userMangaWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 15
}

### Register a second user, to test the ownership check
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manga-tracker-2",
  "password": "supersecret",
  "email": "manga-tracker-2@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("otherMangaTrackerUserId", response.body.id);
%}

### Try updating user 1's tracking record through user 2's path -> expect 404, not 200
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{otherMangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userMangaWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 1
}

### Update a user-work that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5
}

### Stop tracking -> expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userMangaWorkId}}

### Confirm it's gone -> READING tab should be empty again
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{mangaTrackerUserId}}/user-works?status=READING
